From 6c2f957b5982238e6da87ec267aa82b8086b9c92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kyuka Books <dev@kyukabooks.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 20:58:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Rebrand: BookMarketingOS -> Kyuka Books (UI text only)

Renames only user-facing display strings from BookMarketingOS to Kyuka Books:

- Frontend: header/sidebar/footer logo text, page titles & metadata,
  marketing/about/contact/blog copy, auth pages
- Backend: email subject lines shown to users
- Project READMEs

Deliberately UNCHANGED (infrastructure identifiers, not branding):
- Database name (DATABASE_URL, POSTGRES_DB in .env.example,
  docker-compose*.yml, ci.yml)
- S3 bucket name default
- EMAIL_FROM sending domain
- npm package.json 'name'/'description' fields
- Scraper User-Agent header string
- Backend startup log line

Those are operational config, not branding, and renaming them risks
breaking a live database connection, bucket, or deploy pipeline that
still points at the old identifiers.
