From 2b11093d63b33727710415620f56bbd31185b91b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kyuka Books <dev@kyukabooks.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 21:03:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Rebrand PWA manifest + app icons; add TWA assetlinks.json
 template
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

manifest.webmanifest 'name'/'short_name' still said BookMarketingOS and
the theme_color was the old violet — this is what Android shows as the
app name/splash when installed via TWA, so it's genuinely part of the
rebrand (missed by the earlier UI-text patch since .webmanifest/.ico
files aren't matched by the *.json/*.ts file filters used there).

- manifest.webmanifest: name/short_name -> 'Kyuka Books', theme_color
  -> #4338CA (new brand indigo)
- icon-192.png, icon-512.png, icon-512-maskable.png, favicon.ico:
  replaced the old purple 'B' mark with the Kyuka Books open-book icon
  (maskable variant re-checked against the safe-zone requirement)
- Added frontend/public/.well-known/assetlinks.json as a TEMPLATE for
  Digital Asset Links verification, required for a TWA APK to open the
  PWA full-screen without browser chrome. It has two placeholders that
  must be filled in before it does anything:
    - package_name: your TWA's Android applicationId
    - sha256_cert_fingerprints: the SHA256 fingerprint of the keystore
      used to sign the APK (get it via 'keytool -list -v' or from
      PWABuilder/bubblewrap's output)
  Left as placeholders since neither value is knowable from the repo.
